{
  "configuration_id": "config_017",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) achieved 0.527 acc / 0.510 F1, a clear ~4-point gain over RNA-only (config_001: 0.485/0.464), confirming that multimodal fusion with these encoders is beneficial. Image alone (config_010: 0.208) is weak, so the gain comes from complementary information. Uncertainty: We have only tested concat fusion; weighted fusion is untested and could redistribute modality contributions more effectively (especially given the large performance gap between RNA and image). This experiment (config_017) changes exactly one variable—fusion from concat to weighted—while holding model setting, profile setting, RNA encoder, and image encoder identical to config_016. This clean A/B comparison isolates the effect of fusion strategy. If weighted outperforms concat, it identifies a low-cost improvement to carry forward into all future multimodal experiments (multiprofile, alternative encoders). If they are comparable, we can deprioritize fusion and redirect budget toward the larger unexplored dimensions (multiprofile, scvi/scgpt encoders, ViT image encoder). Under a limited budget, this single-variable test maximizes information per experiment."
}

